Review written to `/Users/rich/source/HARES/docs/reviews/air-properties/air-01-isa-standard-pressure-function.md`.

**Summary**: 6 findings (1 medium, 5 low). The ISA formula `p = p0*(1-L·h/T0)^E` is correctly implemented and matches USSA 1976 geometric-altitude values to within 0.005 Pa at all tested altitudes. Key observations:

- HARES's exponent (5.2558761) is more precise than EnergyPlus's (5.2559) by design
- Both HARES and EnergyPlus use geometric altitude (not geopotential), which diverges from USSA 1976 tables by ~12.6 Pa at 3000m — standard building-simulation convention
- The test expected value at 1609 m (83460.0 Pa) deviates from all standard formulas by ~29 Pa — should be verified against a cited source or corrected
- `standard_pressure_pa` lacks an overflow guard present in the duplicate `isa_pressure_kpa` in hares-io
